    "title": "The A Form: The Pentatonic at the Nut",
    "summary": "Five of the A form's six lower dots sit on open strings, and it is the only one of the five windows whose dot count changes by more than one when the quality does.",
    "tags": ["caged", "minor"],
    "readingTimeMin": 3,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-14"
