    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Where the C form put its dots in two clusters at opposite ends of a five-fret window, this one sits still. All twelve dots fall inside four consecutive frets, and — unlike anywhere else in this chapter — the lowest ones don't need a fret at all."
        }
