        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Character, in the reach. Its three-fret strings are 6, 5 and 1 — the outside of the hand stretches, the middle stays compact. And because five of the six lower dots are open, the stretch costs nothing: the open string does the reaching for you. That is worth sitting with, because every other window in this chapter puts the same three-fret reach entirely on fretted fingers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One thing to try before you move on. Hold a sustained "
